-- Cross-file fixture for the MULTI-CLAUSE blind spot (#2651).
-- `stepA` is one function written as two pattern clauses. NEITHER clause alone
-- reaches dupComplexityThreshold, so while the floor was judged per clause this
-- pair was invisible however exactly it duplicated dup_multiclause_b.mdk's
-- `stepB`. Judged on the function, the two clauses together clear the floor and
-- both sides fire. Exported so only rule-duplicate-body has anything to say.
export
stepA : Int -> Int -> String
stepA 0 m = if m > 10 then "many" else "few"
stepA n m = if n > m then "left" else "right"
